@startuml direct-rialto-muxed-ts-attach-sequence
title Muxed HLS-TS: one inject thread attaches every source
skinparam shadowing false

participant "TS inject thread\n(only thread for A+V)" as INJ
participant "AampRialtoPlayer" as PLAYER
participant "Video source" as VS
participant "Audio source" as AS
participant "IMediaPipeline" as PIPE

INJ -> PLAYER : Configure(formats from PMT)
note right of PLAYER
  Sources are created (gate BLOCKED), format recorded with
  setFormat().  A format still UNKNOWN is filled in later by
  TryReuseExistingPipeline() once the codec is identified.
end note
INJ -> PLAYER : SendCopy(VIDEO, first ES frame)
PLAYER -> PLAYER : video not attached -> loop over ALL sources
PLAYER -> PLAYER : SetStreamCaps(VIDEO, codec only)
PLAYER -> VS : attachOrUpdate()
VS -> PIPE : attachSource(MediaSourceVideo)
VS --> PLAYER : NEWLY_ATTACHED
PLAYER -> PLAYER : OnSourceNewlyAttached(): CommitBaseline,\nrelease PositionPending, drain deferred non-video
PLAYER -> PLAYER : SetStreamCaps(AUDIO, codec only)
PLAYER -> AS : attachOrUpdate()
AS -> PIPE : attachSource(MediaSourceAudio)
PLAYER -> PLAYER : CheckAllSourcesAttached()
PLAYER -> PIPE : allSourcesAttached()
PLAYER -> PLAYER : release SourcesNotAttached hold
INJ -> VS : processDataFragment() -> injectOneSample()
note over INJ, PIPE
  Why: with a single thread, if only the video source were
  attached, that thread would block in injectOneSample() waiting
  for a needData and never get to attach audio (code comment:
  "deadlock with muxed HLS-TS which uses only one injection
  thread").  DeferAttachUntilVideo() still orders video first.
end note
@enduml
